-- `emit` is a SUSTAINED emitter: every frame spawns `rate` particles (same random
-- draw order as `burst`) at its point or at the referenced sprite — so the whole
-- particle stream must be bit-identical in both engines.
emit smoke rising at 64, 100 in gray for 90 frames
ship is {x: 20, y: 60, dx: 2}
emitted is no
to update
  ship.x is ship.x + ship.dx
  if ship.x > 100 ship.dx is 0 - ship.dx
  if ship.x < 10 ship.dx is 0 - ship.dx
  if emitted is no
    emit 3 sparks from ship in yellow for 40 frames
    emitted is yes
to draw
  clear screen to black
  draw rect at ship.x, ship.y size 6, 6 in cyan
run game with update and draw
